## Run an instance

```sh
cp instances/example.env instances/mine.env   # fill in NAME_PREFIX, ports, DATA_ROOT{% if gpu %}, GPU_UUIDS{% endif %}
make check INSTANCE=mine
{%- if kind == 'workspace' or build %}
make build INSTANCE=mine    # or set IMAGE_TAG to a published <version>-<variant>
{%- endif %}
make up INSTANCE=mine
```

- Ports bind to `127.0.0.1`. From your machine: `ssh -L <port>:127.0.0.1:<port> <host>`.
{%- if kind == 'workspace' %}
- Connect: `ssh -p <HOST_SSH_PORT> {{ container_user }}@<host>` with a key from `AUTHORIZED_KEYS`. The SSH host key is created on first start and kept in the home volume.
{%- endif %}
{%- if gpu %}
- Pick free GPUs with `nvidia-smi` and pin them by UUID (`nvidia-smi -L`).
{%- endif %}
- `make down` keeps volumes and data. Remove volumes only on purpose: `docker volume ls --filter label=com.docker.compose.project=<project>`.
- Put secrets in `secrets/app.env` (gitignored).
- Need `ipc: host` (some multi-GPU frameworks)? Add it in a local `compose.override.yaml` and check with `COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.override.yaml ALLOW_IPC_HOST=1 make check`.

